    "result": "Perfect! All tests are passing. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\nI fixed two failing tests in the frai-core test suite:\n\n### 1. **Fixed `src/eval/index.test.js` toxicity score error** (`src/eval/index.js`)\n   - **Problem**: The `runEvaluations` function was calling all metrics with `(outputs, references)`, but `toxicityMetric` expects `(outputs, bannedTerms)`. When references were passed as the second parameter, they were treated as banned terms, causing text to be incorrectly flagged.\n   - **Solution**: Added a special case to call `toxicityMetric` with only the outputs parameter, since it doesn't use references.\n\n### 2. **Fixed `src/finetune/governance.test.js` undefined exports error** (`src/finetune/index.js`)\n   - **Problem**: The test imported `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but the module only exported it in the default export, not as a named export.\n   - **Solution**: Added explicit named export statements for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`.\n\n**Results**: All 28 tests across 8 test files now pass \u2713",
